<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:modeler="http://camunda.org/schema/modeler/1.0" id="Definitions_HogaanPromptAssembly" targetNamespace="http://hogaan.app/processes" exporter="Hogaan Process Specification" exporterVersion="1.0" modeler:executionPlatform="Camunda Cloud" modeler:executionPlatformVersion="8.9.0">
  <bpmn:message id="Message_PromptRequest" name="PromptAssemblyRequested" />
  <bpmn:error id="Error_Library" name="LibraryError" errorCode="500" />
  <bpmn:error id="Error_LogWrite" name="LogWriteError" errorCode="500" />
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collaboration_Hogaan_PromptAssembly">
    <bpmn:documentation>Collaboration scope for Prompt Assembly. Single pool ('Hogaan Coaching Platform') with two lanes used: Orchestration Engine and Data Layer. WhatsApp Gateway, LLM Service, and External Services lanes are not used in this process.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:participant id="Participant_Hogaan" name="Hogaan Coaching Platform" processRef="Process_PromptAssembly" />
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_PromptAssembly" name="Hogaan Prompt Assembly Process" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>Hogaan Prompt Assembly Process. The deterministic prompt-construction pipeline invoked by Process #2 (Coaching Conversation) and Process #1 (Onboarding) before any LLM call. Builds the final prompt string from: a system template (selected by responseMode), Hamse's 12-Practice and 4-Level framing injections, voice rules ('useful to society' anchor, asset-based framing, story→insight→action arc), optional Somali cultural framing, retrieved memory, recent session context, the user profile block, and the user's current message.

DESIGN PRINCIPLES:
- Determinism: same inputs always produce the same prompt. No randomness, no clock-dependent values, no implicit context. Step 13 generates a SHA-256 hash of the structural prompt (excluding dynamic slots) so we can verify determinism in tests and debug regressions.
- Brand integrity: voice rules, framing, and cultural context are baked in via DMN-driven business rule tasks (Steps 3-7) reading from the Prompt Templates / Cultural Framing / Voice Rules libraries. These libraries are owned by Process #17 (Prompt and Content Management).
- Token budget enforcement: the assembled prompt is bounded at 4000 tokens. If exceeded, an embedded subprocess runs three sequential degradation strategies — truncate memory, truncate session, drop cultural framing — checking token count after each. If all three are applied and we still exceed, the process terminates at E9 (PromptOversize).
- Mode-aware terminal routing: the same pipeline produces prompts for four distinct response modes (FullCoachingResponse, ProfileUpdateAcknowledgment, ClarifyingQuestion, MetaResponse), each with its own end event so the caller can route accordingly.
- Fail-open logging: prompt log write at Step 14 is fail-open — if logging breaks, the process still returns the assembled prompt to the caller (the prompt was successfully built; logging is a side concern). Note that this contrasts with Process #12 audit logging which is fail-closed for security reasons.

LIBRARY DEPENDENCIES (loaded once at Step 2):
- Prompt Templates library: maps responseMode → system template string
- Cultural Framing library: Somali context cues, contextual proverbs, asset-based reframings
- Voice Rules library: Hamse's tone (warm, pragmatic, story-grounded), 'useful to society' anchor, asset-based language
All three are versioned snapshots resolved at Step 2 — the rest of the pipeline operates on the resolved versions to ensure consistency within a single prompt assembly.

OWNERSHIP: Orchestration Engine runs the entire pipeline including the embedded token budget subprocess. Data Layer hosts Step 2 (library version resolution from Process #17's stores) and Step 14 (prompt log write to async log store). LLM Service is NOT used in this process — this process produces a prompt, it does not call an LLM. WhatsApp Gateway and External Services are not used.

ENGINE TARGET: This artifact is a SPECIFICATION not a deployment. isExecutable=false. Use as the source-of-truth functional spec for service implementation.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_PromptAssembly">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_OrchestrationEngine" name="Orchestration Engine">
        <bpmn:documentation>Orchestration Engine. Hosts the entire prompt-assembly pipeline: input validation, all 5 framing-injection business rule tasks, all 4 context-construction script tasks, user message insertion, the token budget enforcement embedded subprocess, hash generation, output construction, and the mode-routing terminal gateway. Implementation: in-memory pipeline running in the application backend.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>StartEvent_PromptRequested</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Step1_InputValidation</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_InputValid</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>EndEvent_MalformedInput</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_TagsValid</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>EndEvent_PracticeOrLevelTagInvalid</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Step3_SystemPromptSelection</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_TemplateFound</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>EndEvent_TemplateMissing</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Step4_PracticeFramingInjection</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Step5_LevelFramingInjection</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Step6_VoiceRulesInjection</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Step7_CulturalFramingSelection</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Step8_MemoryBlockConstruction</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Step9_SessionContextConstruction</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Step10_UserProfileConstruction</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Step11_UserMessageInsertion</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Step12_TokenBudgetEnforcement</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_BudgetResult</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>EndEvent_PromptOversize</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Step13_HashGeneration</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Step15_OutputErrorPath</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>EndEvent_PromptLogWriteFailed</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Step15_OutputConstruction</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_ModeRouting</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>EndEvent_PromptAssembledNormal</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>EndEvent_PromptAssembledWithDegradation</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>EndEvent_PromptAssembledClarifyMode</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>EndEvent_PromptAssembledMetaMode</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_DataLayer" name="Data Layer">
        <bpmn:documentation>Data Layer. Hosts the two tasks that touch persistent stores: Library Version Resolution (Step 2 — reads from Process #17's prompt template, cultural framing, and voice rules stores) and Prompt Logging (Step 14 — writes to the async prompt log for offline evaluation and regression testing).</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Step2_LibraryVersionResolution</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Event_Error_S2</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>EndEvent_LibraryUnavailable</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Step14_PromptLogging</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Event_Error_S14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>
    <bpmn:dataObject id="DataObject_InputPayload" name="InputPayload" />
    <bpmn:dataObjectReference id="Ref_InputPayload" name="InputPayload" dataObjectRef="DataObject_InputPayload">
      <bpmn:documentation>InputPayload — what arrives from the calling process. Fields: userId, sessionId, responseMode (FullCoachingResponse | ProfileUpdateAcknowledgment | ClarifyingQuestion | MetaResponse), practiceTag (one of 12 practices, optional for some modes), levelTag (Self | Team | Organization | Community, optional), userMessage (the current user input), userProfile (goals, role, tenure, location, isDiaspora), retrievedMemories (array of relevant memory entries from semantic search), sessionTurns (last 3-5 user/assistant turns).</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:dataObjectReference>
    <bpmn:dataObject id="DataObject_ResolvedLib" name="ResolvedLibraryVersions" />
    <bpmn:dataObjectReference id="Ref_ResolvedLib" name="ResolvedLibraryVersions" dataObjectRef="DataObject_ResolvedLib">
      <bpmn:documentation>ResolvedLibraryVersions — output of Step 2. Snapshot pointers to the active library versions used for this assembly. Fields: templateLibVersion, culturalLibVersion, voiceLibVersion, resolvedAt timestamp, libraryHashes (for determinism verification). All subsequent steps in the pipeline operate on these specific versions to ensure the prompt is internally consistent.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:dataObjectReference>
    <bpmn:dataObject id="DataObject_Prompt" name="PromptUnderConstruction" />
    <bpmn:dataObjectReference id="Ref_Prompt" name="PromptUnderConstruction" dataObjectRef="DataObject_Prompt">
      <bpmn:documentation>PromptUnderConstruction — the prompt being built up across Steps 3-11. Mutable across the pipeline. Fields: systemPromptText, practiceFraming, levelFraming, voiceRulesBlock, culturalFramingBlock (may be null if not applicable), memoryBlock, sessionContextBlock, userProfileBlock, userMessageBlock. Final assembled string is concatenation in canonical order.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:dataObjectReference>
    <bpmn:dataObject id="DataObject_TokenCount" name="TokenCount" />
    <bpmn:dataObjectReference id="Ref_TokenCount" name="TokenCount" dataObjectRef="DataObject_TokenCount">
      <bpmn:documentation>TokenCount — output of token counting in Step 12 subprocess. Fields: tokenCount (current count after any truncation), tokenizerModel (e.g., 'cl100k_base'), countAt (timestamp). Recomputed each iteration of the degradation loop.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:dataObjectReference>
    <bpmn:dataObject id="DataObject_Degradation" name="DegradationFlags" />
    <bpmn:dataObjectReference id="Ref_Degradation" name="DegradationFlags" dataObjectRef="DataObject_Degradation">
      <bpmn:documentation>DegradationFlags — tracks which token-budget degradations have been applied. Fields: memTruncated (boolean), sessTruncated (boolean), cultDropped (boolean), exhausted (boolean — true when all three strategies applied and still over budget). Used by the subprocess gateway to determine the next degradation step.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:dataObjectReference>
    <bpmn:dataObject id="DataObject_Hash" name="DeterminismHash" />
    <bpmn:dataObjectReference id="Ref_Hash" name="DeterminismHash" dataObjectRef="DataObject_Hash">
      <bpmn:documentation>DeterminismHash — output of Step 13. SHA-256 hash of the prompt's STRUCTURAL elements (system template, framing, voice rules, cultural framing) excluding dynamic slots (current user message, session turns, memory). Used to verify determinism in tests and detect prompt-template drift between runs.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:dataObjectReference>
    <bpmn:dataObject id="DataObject_Output" name="OutputBundle" />
    <bpmn:dataObjectReference id="Ref_Output" name="OutputBundle" dataObjectRef="DataObject_Output">
      <bpmn:documentation>OutputBundle — final return to caller. Fields: assembledPrompt (the full prompt string ready for LLM call), responseMode (echoed from input), determinismHash, libraryVersionsUsed, degradationFlags (so caller knows if truncation happened), tokenCount, assembledAt timestamp.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:dataObjectReference>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="StartEvent_PromptRequested" name="Prompt Assembly Requested">
      <bpmn:documentation>Process trigger. Invoked by Process #2 (Coaching Conversation) before each LLM call to assemble the prompt, OR by Process #1 (Onboarding) for the personalized confirmation message at Step 8.

PAYLOAD: see DataObject_InputPayload.

EVENT TYPE: Message start event. In implementation this is a synchronous in-process call (the calling process awaits the OutputBundle).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Start_S1</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:messageEventDefinition id="MsgDef_PromptReq" messageRef="Message_PromptRequest" />
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:scriptTask id="Task_Step1_InputValidation" name="Step 1: Validate Input Payload">
      <bpmn:documentation>Step 1 — Input Payload Validation.

PURPOSE: Validate the incoming payload before any library or formatting work. Fail fast on malformed input.

CHECKS:
- userId, sessionId present
- responseMode in [FullCoachingResponse, ProfileUpdateAcknowledgment, ClarifyingQuestion, MetaResponse]
- userMessage present and non-empty
- userProfile present (may have null fields, but the structure must exist)
- For modes that require tags (FullCoachingResponse, ProfileUpdateAcknowledgment): practiceTag and levelTag present
- retrievedMemories and sessionTurns are arrays (may be empty)

OUTPUT: isValid (boolean), validationError (string).

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Pure script task with JSON schema validator. Sub-2ms latency.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Start_S1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_S1_GW1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:scriptTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_InputValid" name="Input Valid?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Routes based on input validation result.

DECISION LOGIC (plain English):
- VALID branch: isValid == true → proceed to Step 2 (Library Resolution)
- INVALID branch: isValid == false → terminate at EndEvent_MalformedInput (E5); caller receives validation error</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_S1_GW1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_InputValid_No</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_InputValid_Yes</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="EndEvent_MalformedInput" name="E5: Malformed Input">
      <bpmn:documentation>E5: MalformedInput. Payload validation failed. Caller receives validationError details. Indicates upstream bug in the calling process — high-severity log entry.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_InputValid_No</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_Step2_LibraryVersionResolution" name="Step 2: Resolve Library Versions">
      <bpmn:documentation>Step 2 — Library Version Resolution.

PURPOSE: Resolve the currently-active versions of the three prompt-related libraries: Prompt Templates, Cultural Framing, Voice Rules. All subsequent steps operate on these specific versions, ensuring the assembled prompt is internally consistent.

LOGIC: Look up the active version pointer for each library from Process #17's library store. Cache hit returns immediately; cache miss triggers a fetch. Each library is independently versioned.

LIBRARIES:
- Prompt Templates: system templates indexed by responseMode
- Cultural Framing: Somali cultural context cues, asset-based reframings
- Voice Rules: Hamse's tone characteristics, language patterns, 'useful to society' anchor phrasings

OUTPUT: resolvedLibrary with version snapshots and hashes.

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Service task with cache layer. p99 5ms cache hit; 35ms on miss. Errors here are infrastructure failures.

TAG VALIDATION: After resolution, validate that the input's practiceTag and levelTag (if required by the mode) exist in the resolved library catalogs. If not, terminate at E7 (PracticeOrLevelTagInvalid).

ERROR BOUNDARY: Library service unavailable routes via Event_Error_S2 to E6 (LibraryUnavailable). Fail-fast — cannot proceed without these libraries.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_InputValid_Yes</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_S2_GW2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="EndEvent_LibraryUnavailable" name="E6: Library Unavailable">
      <bpmn:documentation>E6: LibraryUnavailable. Library service down. Calling process notified. Sustained occurrence indicates infrastructure issue with Process #17's library service.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_S2Error</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_TagsValid" name="Tags Valid?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Validates that the input tags exist in the resolved libraries.

DECISION LOGIC (plain English):
- VALID branch: practiceTag in resolved practices catalog AND levelTag in resolved levels catalog (or tags not required for this mode) → proceed to Step 3
- INVALID branch: tag(s) reference values not present in the catalogs → terminate at E7</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_S2_GW2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_TagsValid_No</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_TagsValid_Yes</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="EndEvent_PracticeOrLevelTagInvalid" name="E7: Practice/Level Tag Invalid">
      <bpmn:documentation>E7: PracticeOrLevelTagInvalid. Input referenced a practice or level tag that doesn't exist in the resolved library catalogs. Indicates either caller bug or library version drift — investigate.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_TagsValid_No</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:businessRuleTask id="Task_Step3_SystemPromptSelection" name="Step 3: Select System Template">
      <bpmn:documentation>Step 3 — System Prompt Template Selection.

PURPOSE: Select the system template string from the Prompt Templates library based on responseMode.

LOGIC: DMN decision table mapping responseMode → systemTemplateText:
- FullCoachingResponse → 'coaching_main_v3' template (~600 tokens)
- ProfileUpdateAcknowledgment → 'profile_ack_v1' template (~150 tokens)
- ClarifyingQuestion → 'clarify_v1' template (~200 tokens)
- MetaResponse → 'meta_v1' template (~300 tokens)

OUTPUT: prompt.systemPromptText populated.

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Business rule task (DMN). Pure lookup against resolvedLibrary.templates. 5ms.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_TagsValid_Yes</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_S3_GW3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:businessRuleTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_TemplateFound" name="Template Found?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Routes based on whether the selected template was actually present.

DECISION LOGIC:
- FOUND branch: template lookup succeeded → proceed to Step 4
- MISSING branch: template ID resolved but not actually present in this library version → terminate at E8. Indicates library catalog inconsistency.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_S3_GW3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Template_No</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Template_Yes</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="EndEvent_TemplateMissing" name="E8: Template Missing">
      <bpmn:documentation>E8: TemplateMissing. Template referenced by responseMode mapping not found in resolved library version. Library catalog inconsistency — engineering investigation required.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Template_No</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:businessRuleTask id="Task_Step4_PracticeFramingInjection" name="Step 4: Inject Practice Framing">
      <bpmn:documentation>Step 4 — Practice Framing Injection (Hamse's 12 Practices).

PURPOSE: Inject the practice-specific framing for the current practiceTag.

LOGIC: DMN lookup mapping practiceTag → practiceFramingBlock. The 12 practices are the foundation of Hamse's framework:
- Self level: Integrity, Purpose, Accountability
- Team level: Dignity, Empathy, Inclusion
- Organization level: Assets, Innovation, Prosperity
- Community level: Humility, Democracy, Peace

Each practice has its own framing block: a short paragraph describing the practice in Hamse's voice, key questions the coach asks, and reframings to apply.

OUTPUT: prompt.practiceFraming populated.

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Pure deterministic lookup. 5ms.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Template_Yes</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_S4_S5</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:businessRuleTask>
    <bpmn:businessRuleTask id="Task_Step5_LevelFramingInjection" name="Step 5: Inject Level Framing">
      <bpmn:documentation>Step 5 — Level Framing Injection (4 Leadership Levels).

PURPOSE: Inject level-specific cues based on the levelTag.

LOGIC: DMN lookup mapping levelTag → levelFramingBlock:
- Self → 'leading the self' cues, focus on integrity and purpose
- Team → 'leading the team' cues, focus on dignity and empathy
- Organization → 'leading the organization' cues, focus on assets and innovation
- Community → 'leading the community' cues, focus on humility and democracy

OUTPUT: prompt.levelFraming populated.

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Pure deterministic lookup. 5ms.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_S4_S5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_S5_S6</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:businessRuleTask>
    <bpmn:businessRuleTask id="Task_Step6_VoiceRulesInjection" name="Step 6: Inject Voice Rules">
      <bpmn:documentation>Step 6 — Voice Rules Injection.

PURPOSE: Inject Hamse's voice characteristics — the brand DNA of every coaching response.

VOICE RULES (from Voice Rules library):
- 'Useful to society' anchor: every response should connect to the larger purpose
- Asset-based language: lead with what people have, not what they lack
- Story → Insight → Values/Cultural Framing → Action arc
- 'From hero to guide' mindset: don't be the hero, help the user become one
- Translate intangible challenges into tangible solutions
- Warm but pragmatic — no false motivational fluff
- Sparing use of Somali phrases when culturally appropriate (controlled by Step 7)

OUTPUT: prompt.voiceRulesBlock populated.

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Pure deterministic lookup. 5ms.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_S5_S6</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_S6_S7</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:businessRuleTask>
    <bpmn:businessRuleTask id="Task_Step7_CulturalFramingSelection" name="Step 7: Select Cultural Framing">
      <bpmn:documentation>Step 7 — Cultural Framing Selection (Conditional).

PURPOSE: Decide whether to add Somali cultural framing to this prompt, and if so, select which cultural cues.

DECISION LOGIC: Evaluates several inputs:
- userProfile.isDiaspora (true if user is outside Horn of Africa)
- responseMode (some modes don't benefit from cultural framing — e.g., MetaResponse)
- practiceTag (some practices map naturally to Somali cultural concepts; others don't)
- userMessage content (does it reference family, community, identity that suggests cultural framing would land?)

If framing should be added: select 1-2 relevant cultural cues from the Cultural Framing library and inject them into prompt.culturalFramingBlock. If not, set culturalFramingBlock to null.

OUTPUT: prompt.culturalFramingBlock populated (or null).

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Business rule task with multi-input DMN table. 15ms.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_S6_S7</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_S7_S8</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:businessRuleTask>
    <bpmn:scriptTask id="Task_Step8_MemoryBlockConstruction" name="Step 8: Build Memory Block">
      <bpmn:documentation>Step 8 — Memory Block Construction.

PURPOSE: Format the retrieved memories into a chronological bullet list for the LLM.

LOGIC: Take retrievedMemories (array of memory entries with timestamps and topics), sort chronologically, format as:
- Markdown bullet list with date stamps
- Each entry summarized to 1-2 sentences
- Older memories pruned if list exceeds N entries (default 10)

OUTPUT: prompt.memoryBlock populated.

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Pure script task. Formatting only. 5ms.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_S7_S8</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_S8_S9</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:scriptTask>
    <bpmn:scriptTask id="Task_Step9_SessionContextConstruction" name="Step 9: Build Session Context">
      <bpmn:documentation>Step 9 — Session Context Construction.

PURPOSE: Format the recent session turns into the User/Assistant exchange format the LLM expects.

LOGIC: Take sessionTurns (last 3-5 turns), interleave as User: / Assistant: blocks in chronological order. This is the immediate context the LLM uses to maintain conversation continuity.

OUTPUT: prompt.sessionContextBlock populated.

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Pure script task. 5ms.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_S8_S9</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_S9_S10</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:scriptTask>
    <bpmn:scriptTask id="Task_Step10_UserProfileConstruction" name="Step 10: Build Profile Block">
      <bpmn:documentation>Step 10 — User Profile Block Construction.

PURPOSE: Format the user profile attributes into a concise reference block for the LLM.

LOGIC: Format goals (mapped practices), role, location/diaspora flag, tenure as a structured paragraph or labeled list. Excludes PII like phone number — uses only the coaching-relevant attributes.

OUTPUT: prompt.userProfileBlock populated.

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Pure script task. 2ms.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_S9_S10</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_S10_S11</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:scriptTask>
    <bpmn:scriptTask id="Task_Step11_UserMessageInsertion" name="Step 11: Insert User Message">
      <bpmn:documentation>Step 11 — User Message Insertion.

PURPOSE: Insert the current user message into the prompt as the final input the LLM responds to.

LOGIC: Apply Unicode normalization (NFC), trim trailing whitespace, then place into prompt.userMessageBlock. NO content modification — the user's message goes through unchanged.

OUTPUT: prompt.userMessageBlock populated. The full prompt is now structurally complete.

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Pure script task. 2ms.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_S10_S11</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_S11_S12</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:scriptTask>
    <bpmn:subProcess id="Task_Step12_TokenBudgetEnforcement" name="Step 12: Token Budget Enforcement">
      <bpmn:documentation>Step 12 — Token Budget Enforcement (Embedded Subprocess).

PURPOSE: Ensure the assembled prompt fits within the 4000-token budget. If oversize, sequentially apply degradation strategies until the budget is met or all strategies are exhausted.

INTERNAL FLOW:
1. Count tokens (using cl100k_base tokenizer or model-equivalent)
2. If &lt;= 4000: exit normally to SubEnd_Complete
3. If &gt; 4000: enter degradation loop:
   a. If memory not yet truncated: truncate memoryBlock to half its current size; loop back to count
   b. If memory truncated and session not yet truncated: truncate sessionContextBlock to last 1-2 turns; loop back
   c. If both truncated and cultural framing still present: drop culturalFramingBlock entirely; loop back
   d. If all three applied and still over budget: exit to SubEnd_Exhausted (sets exhausted=true)

DEGRADATION ORDER RATIONALE: Memory is least critical (LLM still has good baseline knowledge); session context is more critical (conversation continuity); cultural framing is least sacrificable in user-facing terms but is the smallest impact on quality once memory and session are gone.

DEGRADATION FLAGS: Each strategy sets a flag in DegradationFlags so the caller knows what was sacrificed. The OutputBundle includes these flags so Process #2 can decide whether to use the response normally or in 'degraded' mode.

OUTPUT: tokenCount finalized; degradation flags updated.

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Embedded subprocess. p99 ~40ms total (most prompts fit on first count and exit immediately).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_S11_S12</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_S12_GW4</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="SubStart_TokenCheck" name="Begin Enforcement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Internal start of the token budget subprocess.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Sub1</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:scriptTask id="SubTask_CountTokens" name="Count Tokens">
        <bpmn:documentation>Count tokens in the current prompt assembly using the model's tokenizer (cl100k_base for OpenAI-family, or the equivalent for Anthropic). Re-counted each iteration of the degradation loop.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Sub1</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:incoming>Flow_SubLoop1</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:incoming>Flow_SubLoop2</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:incoming>Flow_SubLoop3</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Sub2</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:scriptTask>
      <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="SubGW_BudgetCheck" name="Within Budget?">
        <bpmn:documentation>Routes based on token count.

DECISION LOGIC:
- PASS branch: tokenCount &lt;= 4000 → exit subprocess at SubEnd_Complete
- FAIL branch: tokenCount &gt; 4000 → route to degradation strategy gateway</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Sub2</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Sub_Pass</bpmn:outgoing>
        <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Sub_Fail</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="SubEnd_Complete" name="Enforcement Passed">
        <bpmn:documentation>Token budget enforcement passed. Subprocess exits normally; flow continues at GW_BudgetResult in the parent process.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Sub_Pass</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="SubGW_DegradationStrat" name="Next Degradation?">
        <bpmn:documentation>4-way routing to next degradation strategy based on which have already been applied.

DECISION LOGIC (plain English, evaluated in order):
- MEMORY branch: memTruncated == false → truncate memory next
- SESSION branch: memTruncated == true AND sessTruncated == false → truncate session next
- CULTURAL branch: memTruncated == true AND sessTruncated == true AND cultDropped == false → drop cultural framing next
- EXHAUST branch: all three flags == true → no strategies left; exit at SubEnd_Exhausted</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Sub_Fail</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Strat_Mem</bpmn:outgoing>
        <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Strat_Sess</bpmn:outgoing>
        <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Strat_Cult</bpmn:outgoing>
        <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Strat_Exhaust</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
      <bpmn:scriptTask id="SubTask_TruncateMem" name="Truncate Memory Block">
        <bpmn:documentation>Truncate memoryBlock to half its current entries (oldest first). Sets memTruncated=true. Loops back to recount.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Strat_Mem</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_SubLoop1</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:scriptTask>
      <bpmn:scriptTask id="SubTask_TruncateSess" name="Truncate Session Context">
        <bpmn:documentation>Truncate sessionContextBlock to last 1-2 turns. Sets sessTruncated=true. Loops back to recount.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Strat_Sess</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_SubLoop2</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:scriptTask>
      <bpmn:scriptTask id="SubTask_DropCult" name="Drop Cultural Framing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Drop culturalFramingBlock entirely (set to null). Sets cultDropped=true. Loops back to recount.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Strat_Cult</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_SubLoop3</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:scriptTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="SubEnd_Exhausted" name="Strategies Exhausted">
        <bpmn:documentation>All three degradation strategies applied and prompt still &gt; 4000 tokens. Sets exhausted=true. Parent process will route to E9 (PromptOversize).</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Strat_Exhaust</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Sub1" sourceRef="SubStart_TokenCheck" targetRef="SubTask_CountTokens">
        <bpmn:documentation>Initial entry; count tokens for the assembled prompt.</bpmn:documentation>
      </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Sub2" sourceRef="SubTask_CountTokens" targetRef="SubGW_BudgetCheck">
        <bpmn:documentation>Token count complete; check against 4000 budget.</bpmn:documentation>
      </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Sub_Pass" sourceRef="SubGW_BudgetCheck" targetRef="SubEnd_Complete">
        <bpmn:documentation>Within budget; exit subprocess.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">tokenCount &lt;= 4000</bpmn:conditionExpression>
      </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Sub_Fail" sourceRef="SubGW_BudgetCheck" targetRef="SubGW_DegradationStrat">
        <bpmn:documentation>Over budget; route to next available degradation strategy.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">tokenCount &gt; 4000</bpmn:conditionExpression>
      </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Strat_Mem" sourceRef="SubGW_DegradationStrat" targetRef="SubTask_TruncateMem">
        <bpmn:documentation>Memory not yet truncated; truncate it first.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">memTruncated == false</bpmn:conditionExpression>
      </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Strat_Sess" sourceRef="SubGW_DegradationStrat" targetRef="SubTask_TruncateSess">
        <bpmn:documentation>Memory done, session not yet truncated; truncate session next.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">memTruncated == true AND sessTruncated == false</bpmn:conditionExpression>
      </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Strat_Cult" sourceRef="SubGW_DegradationStrat" targetRef="SubTask_DropCult">
        <bpmn:documentation>Memory and session done; drop cultural framing next.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">memTruncated == true AND sessTruncated == true AND cultDropped == false</bpmn:conditionExpression>
      </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Strat_Exhaust" sourceRef="SubGW_DegradationStrat" targetRef="SubEnd_Exhausted">
        <bpmn:documentation>All three strategies applied and still over budget; exit with exhausted=true.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">cultDropped == true</bpmn:conditionExpression>
      </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_SubLoop1" sourceRef="SubTask_TruncateMem" targetRef="SubTask_CountTokens">
        <bpmn:documentation>Memory truncated; recount tokens.</bpmn:documentation>
      </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_SubLoop2" sourceRef="SubTask_TruncateSess" targetRef="SubTask_CountTokens">
        <bpmn:documentation>Session truncated; recount tokens.</bpmn:documentation>
      </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_SubLoop3" sourceRef="SubTask_DropCult" targetRef="SubTask_CountTokens">
        <bpmn:documentation>Cultural framing dropped; recount tokens.</bpmn:documentation>
      </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    </bpmn:subProcess>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_BudgetResult" name="Budget Exhausted?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Routes based on whether the subprocess succeeded or exhausted.

DECISION LOGIC:
- PASS branch: exhausted == false → proceed to Step 13 (Hash Generation)
- FAIL branch: exhausted == true → terminate at E9 (PromptOversize)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_S12_GW4</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Budget_Fail</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Budget_Pass</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="EndEvent_PromptOversize" name="E9: Prompt Oversize">
      <bpmn:documentation>E9: PromptOversize. Token budget enforcement exhausted all degradation strategies and the prompt still exceeds 4000 tokens. Indicates either an unusually large user message OR a structural issue with the prompt template. Calling process should fall back to a templated (non-LLM) response.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Budget_Fail</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:scriptTask id="Task_Step13_HashGeneration" name="Step 13: Generate Determinism Hash">
      <bpmn:documentation>Step 13 — Determinism Hash Generation.

PURPOSE: Generate SHA-256 hash of the prompt's structural elements (system template, framing, voice rules, cultural framing) excluding dynamic slots (current user message, session turns, memory).

USE CASES:
- Determinism verification: same inputs at the structural level always produce the same hash
- Prompt regression detection: if the hash changes unexpectedly, a library version drifted
- A/B test cohort assignment: hash modulo bucket count

OUTPUT: determinismHash (64 hex chars).

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Pure script task. SHA-256 over canonical concatenation of structural blocks. 2ms.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Budget_Pass</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_S13_S14</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:scriptTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_Step14_PromptLogging" name="Step 14: Log Prompt (Async, Fail-Open)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Step 14 — Prompt Log Write (Async, FAIL-OPEN).

PURPOSE: Write the assembled prompt to the prompt log store for offline evaluation, regression testing, and debugging.

LOGIC: Async write to log store with userId, sessionId, responseMode, assembledPrompt (encrypted), tokenCount, degradationFlags, libraryVersionsUsed, determinismHash, timestamp. PII is hashed/masked before storage.

OUTPUT: logEntryId.

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Service task. Write may be deferred via queue. 10ms target.

ERROR BOUNDARY: If logging fails, the process MUST still return the assembled prompt to the caller — the prompt was successfully built; logging is a side concern. The error boundary routes to a separate output construction path (Task_Step15_OutputErrorPath) that builds the output bundle WITH the assembled prompt and ALSO sets a logging-failed flag, then terminates at E10. The caller can use the prompt; engineering is alerted to the logging failure separately.

CONTRAST: Process #12 (User Auth) audit logging is fail-CLOSED for security. This Step 14 logging is fail-OPEN because prompt logs are diagnostic, not security-critical.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_S13_S14</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_S14_S15</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:boundaryEvent id="Event_Error_S2" name="Library Error" attachedToRef="Task_Step2_LibraryVersionResolution">
      <bpmn:documentation>Error boundary on Step 2. Catches LibraryError when the prompt-content library service is unreachable. Routes to E6. The calling process should retry; engineering alerted on sustained failures.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_S2Error</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:errorEventDefinition id="ErrDef_S2" errorRef="Error_Library" />
    </bpmn:boundaryEvent>
    <bpmn:boundaryEvent id="Event_Error_S14" name="Log Write Error" attachedToRef="Task_Step14_PromptLogging">
      <bpmn:documentation>Error boundary on Step 14. Catches LogWriteError. Routes to Task_Step15_OutputErrorPath which still constructs and returns the output bundle with the assembled prompt — fail-open semantics.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_S14Error</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:errorEventDefinition id="ErrDef_S14" errorRef="Error_LogWrite" />
    </bpmn:boundaryEvent>
    <bpmn:scriptTask id="Task_Step15_OutputErrorPath" name="Build Output (Logging Failed)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Output construction on the logging-failure path.

PURPOSE: Even if logging failed, build the OutputBundle so the caller still receives the assembled prompt. Sets logWriteFailed=true flag in the bundle metadata.

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Pure script task; same logic as Task_Step15_OutputConstruction with one extra flag.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_S14Error</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Err_E10</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:scriptTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="EndEvent_PromptLogWriteFailed" name="E10: Prompt Log Write Failed">
      <bpmn:documentation>E10: PromptLogWriteFailed. Prompt successfully assembled and returned to caller, BUT prompt log write failed (caller still got a usable prompt). Engineering alerted to investigate logging infrastructure.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Err_E10</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:scriptTask id="Task_Step15_OutputConstruction" name="Step 15: Construct Output Bundle">
      <bpmn:documentation>Step 15 — Output Bundle Construction (Happy Path).

PURPOSE: Bundle the assembled prompt and all metadata into the OutputBundle returned to the caller.

LOGIC: Concatenate prompt blocks in canonical order to produce assembledPrompt. Include responseMode (echoed from input), determinismHash, libraryVersionsUsed, degradationFlags, tokenCount, assembledAt timestamp.

OUTPUT: OutputBundle ready for return.

IMPLEMENTATION HINT: Pure script task. 2ms.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_S14_S15</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_S15_GW5</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:scriptTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_ModeRouting" name="Response Mode Terminal Routing">
      <bpmn:documentation>Final terminal routing by response mode and degradation status.

DECISION LOGIC (plain English):
- NORMAL branch: responseMode in (FullCoachingResponse, ProfileUpdateAcknowledgment) AND degraded == false → terminate at E1 (PromptAssembledNormal)
- DEGRADED branch: responseMode in (FullCoachingResponse, ProfileUpdateAcknowledgment) AND degraded == true → terminate at E2 (PromptAssembledWithDegradation); caller knows truncation happened
- CLARIFY branch: responseMode == ClarifyingQuestion → terminate at E3 (PromptAssembledClarifyMode)
- META branch: responseMode == MetaResponse → terminate at E4 (PromptAssembledMetaMode)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_S15_GW5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Mode_Normal</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Mode_Degraded</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Mode_Clarify</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_Mode_Meta</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="EndEvent_PromptAssembledNormal" name="E1: Prompt Assembled Normal">
      <bpmn:documentation>E1: PromptAssembledNormal. Standard happy path — prompt assembled within budget for FullCoachingResponse or ProfileUpdateAcknowledgment mode. Caller proceeds to LLM call with full context.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Mode_Normal</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="EndEvent_PromptAssembledWithDegradation" name="E2: Prompt Assembled With Degradation">
      <bpmn:documentation>E2: PromptAssembledWithDegradation. Same as E1 but token budget enforcement applied truncation. Caller knows the prompt is degraded and may consider this when interpreting the LLM response.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Mode_Degraded</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="EndEvent_PromptAssembledClarifyMode" name="E3: Prompt Assembled Clarify Mode">
      <bpmn:documentation>E3: PromptAssembledClarifyMode. Prompt assembled for ClarifyingQuestion mode. Caller will use this to ask the user a focused follow-up rather than provide a full coaching response.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Mode_Clarify</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="EndEvent_PromptAssembledMetaMode" name="E4: Prompt Assembled Meta Mode">
      <bpmn:documentation>E4: PromptAssembledMetaMode. Prompt assembled for MetaResponse mode. Caller will use this for replies about the system itself (e.g., 'what can you help me with?', 'who built you?').</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_Mode_Meta</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Start_S1" sourceRef="StartEvent_PromptRequested" targetRef="Task_Step1_InputValidation">
      <bpmn:documentation>Prompt assembly request received from caller (typically Process #2 Coaching).</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_S1_GW1" sourceRef="Task_Step1_InputValidation" targetRef="GW_InputValid">
      <bpmn:documentation>Validation result; route by isValid.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_InputValid_No" sourceRef="GW_InputValid" targetRef="EndEvent_MalformedInput">
      <bpmn:documentation>Malformed payload; terminate at E5. Caller receives validationError.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">Payload invalid (isValid == false)</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_InputValid_Yes" sourceRef="GW_InputValid" targetRef="Task_Step2_LibraryVersionResolution">
      <bpmn:documentation>Payload OK; resolve current library versions.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">Payload valid (isValid == true)</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_S2_GW2" sourceRef="Task_Step2_LibraryVersionResolution" targetRef="GW_TagsValid">
      <bpmn:documentation>Libraries resolved; validate input tags against catalogs.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_S2Error" sourceRef="Event_Error_S2" targetRef="EndEvent_LibraryUnavailable">
      <bpmn:documentation>Library service unreachable; terminate at E6.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_TagsValid_No" sourceRef="GW_TagsValid" targetRef="EndEvent_PracticeOrLevelTagInvalid">
      <bpmn:documentation>Practice or level tag not found in resolved library; terminate at E7.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">Tag(s) not in catalog (tagsValid == false)</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_TagsValid_Yes" sourceRef="GW_TagsValid" targetRef="Task_Step3_SystemPromptSelection">
      <bpmn:documentation>Tags valid; select system template.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">All tags valid (tagsValid == true)</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_S3_GW3" sourceRef="Task_Step3_SystemPromptSelection" targetRef="GW_TemplateFound">
      <bpmn:documentation>Template selection complete; verify template exists.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Template_No" sourceRef="GW_TemplateFound" targetRef="EndEvent_TemplateMissing">
      <bpmn:documentation>Template ID resolved but not present in current library version; terminate at E8.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">Template missing from library version (templateFound == false)</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Template_Yes" sourceRef="GW_TemplateFound" targetRef="Task_Step4_PracticeFramingInjection">
      <bpmn:documentation>Template found; inject practice framing.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">Template present (templateFound == true)</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_S4_S5" sourceRef="Task_Step4_PracticeFramingInjection" targetRef="Task_Step5_LevelFramingInjection">
      <bpmn:documentation>Practice framing injected; inject level framing.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_S5_S6" sourceRef="Task_Step5_LevelFramingInjection" targetRef="Task_Step6_VoiceRulesInjection">
      <bpmn:documentation>Level framing injected; inject voice rules.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_S6_S7" sourceRef="Task_Step6_VoiceRulesInjection" targetRef="Task_Step7_CulturalFramingSelection">
      <bpmn:documentation>Voice rules injected; evaluate cultural framing.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_S7_S8" sourceRef="Task_Step7_CulturalFramingSelection" targetRef="Task_Step8_MemoryBlockConstruction">
      <bpmn:documentation>Cultural framing applied (or omitted); construct memory block.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_S8_S9" sourceRef="Task_Step8_MemoryBlockConstruction" targetRef="Task_Step9_SessionContextConstruction">
      <bpmn:documentation>Memory block built; construct session context.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_S9_S10" sourceRef="Task_Step9_SessionContextConstruction" targetRef="Task_Step10_UserProfileConstruction">
      <bpmn:documentation>Session context built; construct user profile block.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_S10_S11" sourceRef="Task_Step10_UserProfileConstruction" targetRef="Task_Step11_UserMessageInsertion">
      <bpmn:documentation>Profile block built; insert current user message.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_S11_S12" sourceRef="Task_Step11_UserMessageInsertion" targetRef="Task_Step12_TokenBudgetEnforcement">
      <bpmn:documentation>Prompt structurally complete; enforce token budget.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_S12_GW4" sourceRef="Task_Step12_TokenBudgetEnforcement" targetRef="GW_BudgetResult">
      <bpmn:documentation>Token budget enforcement done; check whether degradation strategies were exhausted.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Budget_Fail" sourceRef="GW_BudgetResult" targetRef="EndEvent_PromptOversize">
      <bpmn:documentation>Cannot fit within 4000 tokens; terminate at E9. Caller falls back to templated response.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">All degradations applied AND still over budget (exhausted == true)</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Budget_Pass" sourceRef="GW_BudgetResult" targetRef="Task_Step13_HashGeneration">
      <bpmn:documentation>Within budget; generate determinism hash.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">Within budget after enforcement (exhausted == false)</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_S13_S14" sourceRef="Task_Step13_HashGeneration" targetRef="Task_Step14_PromptLogging">
      <bpmn:documentation>Hash generated; log the prompt for offline evaluation.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_S14_S15" sourceRef="Task_Step14_PromptLogging" targetRef="Task_Step15_OutputConstruction">
      <bpmn:documentation>Logging succeeded; construct output bundle (happy path).</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_S14Error" sourceRef="Event_Error_S14" targetRef="Task_Step15_OutputErrorPath">
      <bpmn:documentation>Logging failed; build output bundle anyway (FAIL-OPEN — prompt is still returned to caller).</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Err_E10" sourceRef="Task_Step15_OutputErrorPath" targetRef="EndEvent_PromptLogWriteFailed">
      <bpmn:documentation>Output built with logWriteFailed flag; terminate at E10.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_S15_GW5" sourceRef="Task_Step15_OutputConstruction" targetRef="GW_ModeRouting">
      <bpmn:documentation>Output bundle ready; route to mode-specific terminal end event.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Mode_Normal" sourceRef="GW_ModeRouting" targetRef="EndEvent_PromptAssembledNormal">
      <bpmn:documentation>Standard happy path; terminate at E1.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">Coaching/Acknowledgment mode AND not degraded</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Mode_Degraded" sourceRef="GW_ModeRouting" targetRef="EndEvent_PromptAssembledWithDegradation">
      <bpmn:documentation>Truncation applied; terminate at E2; caller informed.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">Coaching/Acknowledgment mode AND degraded == true</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Mode_Clarify" sourceRef="GW_ModeRouting" targetRef="EndEvent_PromptAssembledClarifyMode">
      <bpmn:documentation>Terminate at E3.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">responseMode == ClarifyingQuestion</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Mode_Meta" sourceRef="GW_ModeRouting" targetRef="EndEvent_PromptAssembledMetaMode">
      <bpmn:documentation>Terminate at E4.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">responseMode == MetaResponse</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
  </bpmn:process>
